[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605173000-pds-did-web-resolution-worker", :adr/title "ADR-2605173000: did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com resolution via path-specific Cloudflare Worker", :adr/status "active", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605173000: did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com resolution via path-specific Cloudflare Worker\n\n## Context\n\nThe etzhayyim Personal Data Server (`@atproto/pds@0.4.222`) was deployed on the `simeon` Mac mini and exposed publicly at `https://pds.etzhayyim.com` via a Cloudflare tunnel CNAME (tunnel `178e0a1b-dd7e-480e-bb01-eb100524a58e`, ingress → `http://simeonnomac-mini.local:2583`). ADR-2605172800 § \"PDS at pds.etzhayyim.com\" records the bring-up.\n\nThe service identifier for this PDS is `did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com`. Per the [did:web spec](https://w3c-ccg.github.io/did-method-web/) and the AT Protocol spec, clients resolve a service DID by GET-ing:\n\n```\nhttps://pds.etzhayyim.com/.well-known/did.json\n```\n\nBut the upstream `@atproto/pds` Node binary **does not serve `/.well-known/did.json`**. It serves `/xrpc/*` and a tiny `/_health` endpoint, and 404s on everything else. So even though the host name and TLS terminate correctly through the tunnel, the DID document is unreachable, and `did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com` does not resolve.\n\nThree options:\n\n1. **Patch / fork @atproto/pds** to serve did.json. Rejected — drifts from upstream, makes future PDS upgrades painful, and there's no upstream interest in adding this (the upstream PDS uses `did:plc:*` for service identity, not `did:web:*`).\n2. **Reverse-proxy with a different layer** (e.g., Caddy in front of Bun on simeon). Rejected — adds a moving part on a Mac mini that is supposed to stay minimal, and the simeon host has no public TLS termination of its own (CF tunnel terminates TLS at the edge).\n3. **Path-specific Cloudflare Worker** that owns exactly `pds.etzhayyim.com/.well-known/did.json` and lets every other path fall through to the tunnel CNAME. Accepted.\n\nOption 3 is the same pattern we already use at the apex domain: `50-infra/etzhayyim-did-web/` serves `etzhayyim.com/.well-known/did.json` and everything else on `etzhayyim.com` falls through to other Workers and DNS records.\n\n## Decision\n\n**`did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com` resolves via a path-specific Cloudflare Worker (`etzhayyim-pds-did-web`) bound to the route `pds.etzhayyim.com/.well-known/did.json`. All other paths on `pds.etzhayyim.com` continue to fall through to the CF tunnel CNAME → `simeon:2583` PDS, unchanged.**\n\n### Worker contract\n\n- **Repo path:** `50-infra/etzhayyim-pds-did-web/`\n- **Route:** `pds.etzhayyim.com/.well-known/did.json` (zone `etzhayyim.com`)\n- **Methods:** `GET`, `HEAD` → 200; everything else → 405\n- **Other Worker paths:** 404 (the route binding only matches the one URL, but the handler is defensive)\n- **Response headers:**\n  - `content-type: application/did+json; charset=utf-8`\n  - `cache-control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate`\n  - `access-control-allow-origin: *`\n  - `strict-transport-security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains`\n  - `x-content-type-options: nosniff`\n\n### did.json contract (v1)\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"@context\": [\n    \"https://www.w3.org/ns/did/v1\",\n    \"https://w3id.org/security/multikey/v1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com\",\n  \"alsoKnownAs\": [\"https://pds.etzhayyim.com\"],\n  \"verificationMethod\": [],\n  \"service\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"#atproto_pds\",\n      \"type\": \"AtprotoPersonalDataServer\",\n      \"serviceEndpoint\": \"https://pds.etzhayyim.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nRationale for each field:\n\n- **`id`** — fixed by the route + did:web spec.\n- **`alsoKnownAs`** — the canonical HTTPS URL, so resolvers can dereference the host as well as the DID.\n- **`verificationMethod: []`** — empty in v1. The PDS asserts identity via TLS terminated by Cloudflare; we have no signed service-level assertions yet. When PDS-to-PDS federation messages or relay handshakes need signatures, we'll add a Multikey entry derived from `PDS_PLC_ROTATION_KEY_K256` (stored in 1Password `etzhayyim/pds-simeon/secrets-2026-05-17`). Spec note: AT Protocol clients do not currently require this field to be populated.\n- **`service[#atproto_pds]`** — the AT Protocol mandatory service descriptor. Type and `id` fragment are spec-fixed.\n\n### Fall-through guarantee\n\nThe Worker route is **path-specific** (`/.well-known/did.json`, not `/.well-known/*` and not `*`). For every other path on `pds.etzhayyim.com`, Cloudflare's request router skips the Worker and uses the proxied CNAME record (`pds → 178e0a1b-dd7e-480e-bb01-eb100524a58e.cfargotunnel.com`) to reach the simeon PDS. This is verified by direct request against `/xrpc/_health` and `/xrpc/com.atproto.server.describeServer` continuing to return PDS responses after the Worker is deployed.\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- `did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com` resolves cleanly via direct HTTP and via the W3C Universal Resolver (`https://dev.uniresolver.io/1.0/identifiers/did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com`). Verified 2026-05-17T12:21:27Z.\n- Upstream `@atproto/pds` stays unmodified — future version bumps (0.4.223+, 0.5.x) are clean.\n- The simeon Mac mini stays minimal: just Bun + PDS + tunnel sidecar. No reverse proxy, no extra TLS, no Worker code running on a residential ISP.\n- Edge-cached did.json — 5-minute CDN cache reduces load on the (single) DID lookup path.\n\n### Negative\n\n- did.json updates require a Worker redeploy (`wrangler deploy`) rather than just editing a file on simeon. Acceptable — the did.json is supposed to be stable; rapid churn would be a sign of something wrong.\n- A Worker route can be silently broken by misconfiguration (wrong pattern, wrong zone). Mitigated by smoke test in the `wrangler deploy` flow (`curl /.well-known/did.json` must return 200 with `application/did+json` before declaring deploy successful).\n\n### Neutral\n\n- Two artifacts now own pieces of `pds.etzhayyim.com`: the CNAME for everything, and this Worker for one path. Discoverable through the SSoT: `deps.toml [platform.pds].did_web_*` fields point at the Worker, and the Worker's `wrangler.toml` documents the route + fall-through rule inline.\n\n## Implementation\n\n```\n50-infra/etzhayyim-pds-did-web/\n├── README.edn           # explains why this exists + deploy steps\n├── did.json            # the DID document (v1, minimal)\n├── package.json        # wrangler + types\n├── src/worker.ts       # GET/HEAD → did.json, else 405/404\n├── tsconfig.json       # resolveJsonModule for the import\n└── wrangler.toml       # route pds.etzhayyim.com/.well-known/did.json\n```\n\nDeploy:\n\n```bash\ncd 50-infra/etzhayyim-pds-did-web\nnpm install\nwrangler deploy\n```\n\nVerify:\n\n```bash\ncurl -i https://pds.etzhayyim.com/.well-known/did.json\n# HTTP/2 200, content-type: application/did+json\ncurl https://dev.uniresolver.io/1.0/identifiers/did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com\n# {\"didDocument\":{\"id\":\"did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com\",…}}\n```\n\n## SSoT pointer\n\n- Worker artifact + did.json: `50-infra/etzhayyim-pds-did-web/`\n- Deploy state: `deps.toml [platform.pds].did_web_*`\n- Sister Worker (apex): `50-infra/etzhayyim-did-web/`\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605173000-pds-did-web-resolution-worker.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "pds-did-web-resolution-worker", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-17", :adr/date "2026-05-17", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/authoritative_for ["how `did:web:pds.etzhayyim.com` resolves" "the Worker route that owns `pds.etzhayyim.com/.well-known/did.json`" "the rule that all other `pds.etzhayyim.com/*` paths fall through to the tunnel CNAME" "the did.json contents (id / alsoKnownAs / service[#atproto_pds])" "the verificationMethod posture (empty in v1, TLS-only at this layer)"]}]
